From 7a8bc6d88b1894ceb7f3f3d09f27fdb3860eff5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dastbe <dastbe@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:25:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] starlark: add 'name = load("module", ...)' to bind a module
 value

Behind the new syntax.FileOptions.LoadModule option, a load statement
may appear as the right-hand side of an assignment to a single
identifier. Whereas an ordinary load binds the listed names in the
file scope, the assignment form binds them as attributes of a
*starlark.LoadedModule assigned to the identifier:

    lib = load("lib.star", "f", h="g")   # lib.f, lib.h
    lib = load("lib.star")                 # all exported names

The name list may be omitted only in the assignment form, in which case
the module value has every exported (non-underscore) member.

- syntax: LoadStmt.Alias; parser accepts IDENT '=' load(...)
- resolve: Alias is bound like any other load binding; listed names
  are attributes, not file-scope bindings
- compile: new LOADMODULE<n> opcode; bytecode Version 15
- starlark: LoadedModule value; LOAD/LOADMODULE share Thread.load

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RQkJsyThCiRZxeZr2ymEyZ
